Hi everyone,

I have a problem in my model-averaging beta estimates in my single season occupancy models. Let me explain:

I made several models for three species (Sp1, Sp2 and Sp3). I used five variables for modeling occupancy in each species, four continuous variables (distance of permanent river, dist. paved road, dist. village, elevation) and one categorical variable (vegetation type). As well, I did a shrinking model-averaging beta estimates for each group of models for each species. The sample size were 28, 28, 23 for Sp1, Sp2 and Sp3, respectively. I used ten sampling occasions for each detection history for each species. However, the percentages of missing observations were different: Sp1 had 0.45, Sp2 had 0.46 and Sp3 had 0.35.

The models and its AIC values were:

1.- Sp1 models:

Model nPars    AIC   delta   AICwt   cumltvWt

v2       4   169.70   0.00   0.3919     0.39

v3      4   169.81   0.11   0.3708     0.76

