The large negative estimates for colonization (-7.25 and -8.28) are due to there being no instances where the observed occupancy status goes from 0 to 1.  So the maximum likelihood estimate of the colonization probability is really 0 (with the logit of the colonization probability being minus infinity).  (And because of the stopping rules of the iterative process of the algorithm, it stops at the values you see.)

